// "Destroy [permanent]" ([CR#701.8a]): the keyword action as DATA — a
// `Composite` whose tag is `Destroy(x)` and whose body IS the Battlefield →
// owner's-graveyard `Move`. There is no bespoke `Destroy` verb; the engine
// reads the body facet ("→Graveyard") off this stored move and commits it
// atomically on the one present-tense `Act(Destroy)` event (dual-facet:
// indestructible cants it, regeneration / Rest-in-Peace replace it, all on the
// SAME event — [CR#616.1,702.12b,701.19a]).
//
// The param is a `Reference` (the patient — `This`, a bound `Target`, `It`). It
// appears in BOTH the tag and the body's `Move` source, so the composite's
// realized shape matches its expanded body. Template "destroy ${0}" renders the
// reference context-aware ("Destroy target creature." — sentence-start
// capitalization is the renderer's; templates stay lowercase like every
// sibling verb macro).
//
// Usage: Destroy(This) / Destroy(It) / Destroy(Target(0)).
(
    name: "Destroy",
    template: "destroy ${0}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Reference],
    body: Composite(
        Destroy(Param(0)),
        Move(Param(0), Graveyard),
    ),
)
